          <note>He was the pupil of Nṛsiṁhāśramin (also known as Nṛsiṁhāśramayogin), who was the author of the Tattvaviveka. (See New Catalogus Catalogorum (NCC): vol. 2, p. 47a.)</note>
          <note>He was of the Harita gotra, and was described as the crest-jewel of Cola land and as ‘Sarvatantra-pravartaka’. (See New Catalogus Catalogorum (NCC): vol. 2, p. 393b.)</note>
